IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `ccc-core`
IMPORT `ccc20-part16-interpretation`
IMPORT `ccc20-part16-interim-release`
IMPORT `ccc20-tests-fixtures`

-- ccc20-tests-interim-release.l4 -- tests for ccc20-part16-interim-release.l4 (s 515 apart from (4.1) to (4.4), (6), (6.1), (7), (10); ss 515.01 to 519.1). Expected values are hand-written from the text of lines 11366-11572.

§ `Tests -- section 515(1) and (2)`
-- (1) args: s 469 listing; taken before a justice; a plea of guilty accepted; the prosecutor shows cause (detention justified, or another order)
#ASSERT `s 515(1) the justice must make a release order without conditions` (JUST FALSE) TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 515(1) the justice must make a release order without conditions` NOTHING TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 515(1) the justice must make a release order without conditions` (JUST TRUE) TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 515(1) the justice must make a release order without conditions` (JUST FALSE) FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 515(1) the justice must make a release order without conditions` (JUST FALSE) TRUE TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 515(1) the justice must make a release order without conditions` (JUST FALSE) TRUE FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- (2) args: the justice does not make an order under (1); the prosecutor shows cause why detention is justified
#ASSERT `s 515(2) the justice must make a release order that sets out the conditions directed under subsection (4)` TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 515(2) the justice must make a release order that sets out the conditions directed under subsection (4)` TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 515(2) the justice must make a release order that sets out the conditions directed under subsection (4)` FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- (2)(a) to (e) args: the term; the accused is not ordinarily resident in the province or does not reside within 200 km of the place of custody
#ASSERT `s 515(2) the release order is to set out the financial term` `s 515(2)(a) an indication that the release order does not include any financial obligations` FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 515(2) the release order is to set out the financial term` `s 515(2)(b) the accused's promise to pay a specified amount if they fail to comply with a condition of the order` FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 515(2) the release order is to set out the financial term` `s 515(2)(c) the obligation to have one or more sureties, with or without the accused's promise to pay a specified amount` FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 515(2) the release order is to set out the financial term` `s 515(2)(d) the obligation to deposit money or other valuable security in a specified amount or value, with or without the accused's promise to pay a specified amount` FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 515(2) the release order is to set out the financial term` `s 515(2)(e) the obligation of an accused who is not ordinarily resident in the province, or does not ordinarily reside within 200 kilometres, to deposit money or other valuable security, with or without a promise to pay and with or without sureties` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 515(2) the release order is to set out the financial term` `s 515(2)(e) the obligation of an accused who is not ordinarily resident in the province, or does not ordinarily reside within 200 kilometres, to deposit money or other valuable security, with or without a promise to pay and with or without sureties` FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
-- the outcome. args: s 469 listing; a plea of guilty accepted; the answer of (6); the accused shows cause; the prosecutor shows cause (detention); the prosecutor shows cause (another order); the term
#ASSERT `s 515 the interim release outcome the accused was given` (JUST FALSE) FALSE (JUST FALSE) FALSE FALSE FALSE `s 515(2)(a) an indication that the release order does not include any financial obligations` EQUALS JUST `release on a release order without conditions`
#ASSERT `s 515 the interim release outcome the accused was given` (JUST FALSE) FALSE (JUST FALSE) FALSE FALSE TRUE `s 515(2)(b) the accused's promise to pay a specified amount if they fail to comply with a condition of the order` EQUALS JUST `release on a release order with conditions`
#ASSERT `s 515 the interim release outcome the accused was given` (JUST FALSE) FALSE (JUST FALSE) FALSE FALSE TRUE `s 515(2)(c) the obligation to have one or more sureties, with or without the accused's promise to pay a specified amount` EQUALS JUST `release on a release order with conditions and a surety`
#ASSERT `s 515 the interim release outcome the accused was given` (JUST FALSE) FALSE (JUST FALSE) FALSE FALSE TRUE `s 515(2)(d) the obligation to deposit money or other valuable security in a specified amount or value, with or without the accused's promise to pay a specified amount` EQUALS JUST `release on a release order with conditions`
#ASSERT `s 515 the interim release outcome the accused was given` (JUST FALSE) FALSE (JUST FALSE) FALSE FALSE TRUE `s 515(2)(e) the obligation of an accused who is not ordinarily resident in the province, or does not ordinarily reside within 200 kilometres, to deposit money or other valuable security, with or without a promise to pay and with or without sureties` EQUALS JUST `release on a release order with conditions`
#ASSERT `s 515 the interim release outcome the accused was given` (JUST FALSE) FALSE (JUST FALSE) FALSE TRUE FALSE `s 515(2)(a) an indication that the release order does not include any financial obligations` EQUALS JUST `detention in custody`
#ASSERT `s 515 the interim release outcome the accused was given` (JUST FALSE) FALSE (JUST FALSE) FALSE TRUE TRUE `s 515(2)(b) the accused's promise to pay a specified amount if they fail to comply with a condition of the order` EQUALS JUST `detention in custody`
#ASSERT `s 515 the interim release outcome the accused was given` (JUST TRUE) FALSE (JUST FALSE) FALSE FALSE FALSE `s 515(2)(a) an indication that the release order does not include any financial obligations` EQUALS JUST `detention in custody`
#ASSERT `s 515 the interim release outcome the accused was given` NOTHING FALSE (JUST FALSE) FALSE FALSE FALSE `s 515(2)(a) an indication that the release order does not include any financial obligations` EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 515 the interim release outcome the accused was given` (JUST FALSE) TRUE (JUST FALSE) FALSE FALSE FALSE `s 515(2)(a) an indication that the release order does not include any financial obligations` EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 515 the interim release outcome the accused was given` (JUST FALSE) FALSE (JUST TRUE) FALSE FALSE FALSE `s 515(2)(a) an indication that the release order does not include any financial obligations` EQUALS JUST `detention in custody`
#ASSERT `s 515 the interim release outcome the accused was given` (JUST FALSE) FALSE (JUST TRUE) TRUE FALSE FALSE `s 515(2)(b) the accused's promise to pay a specified amount if they fail to comply with a condition of the order` EQUALS JUST `release on a release order with conditions`
#ASSERT `s 515 the interim release outcome the accused was given` (JUST FALSE) FALSE (JUST TRUE) TRUE FALSE FALSE `s 515(2)(c) the obligation to have one or more sureties, with or without the accused's promise to pay a specified amount` EQUALS JUST `release on a release order with conditions and a surety`
#ASSERT `s 515 the interim release outcome the accused was given` (JUST FALSE) FALSE (JUST TRUE) TRUE TRUE FALSE `s 515(2)(b) the accused's promise to pay a specified amount if they fail to comply with a condition of the order` EQUALS JUST `release on a release order with conditions`
#ASSERT `s 515 the interim release outcome the accused was given` (JUST FALSE) FALSE NOTHING FALSE FALSE FALSE `s 515(2)(a) an indication that the release order does not include any financial obligations` EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 515 the accused is bound by a release order` `release on a release order without conditions` EQUALS TRUE
#ASSERT `s 515 the accused is bound by a release order` `release on a release order with conditions` EQUALS TRUE
#ASSERT `s 515 the accused is bound by a release order` `release on a release order with conditions and a surety` EQUALS TRUE
#ASSERT `s 515 the accused is bound by a release order` `detention in custody` EQUALS FALSE

§ `Tests -- section 515(2.01) to (2.12)`
-- (2.01) args: the term; the prosecution shows cause why a less onerous form would be inadequate; the answer of (6)
