#ASSERT `s 515(4) the justice may direct the accused to comply with the condition` TRUE `s 515(4)(g) comply with any other specified condition that the justice considers necessary to ensure the safety and security of any victim of or witness to the offence` FALSE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 515(4) the justice may direct the accused to comply with the condition` TRUE `s 515(4)(h) comply with any other reasonable conditions specified in the order that the justice considers desirable` FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 515(4) the justice may direct the accused to comply with the condition` TRUE `s 515(4)(h) comply with any other reasonable conditions specified in the order that the justice considers desirable` FALSE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 515(4) the justice may direct the accused to comply with the condition` FALSE `s 515(4)(a) report at specified times to a peace officer, or other person, designated in the order` FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE   -- RECONCILED 2026-11-12: was `s 515(4) the justice may direct the accused to comply with the condition` FALSE `s 515(4)(a) report at specified times to a peace officer, or other person, designated in the order` FALSE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING; the "when" gate on a "may" is the periods ruling (b): the function now answers the guide's JUST FALSE (the other reading is NOTHING, listed in the name-test sweep)

